s impact on investment in the industry, and its impact on energy prices, despite having had more than six months to do so, and* >>> >>> *(iii) that the cynical and absurd stapling of changes to the Petroleum Resource Rent Tax to measures with cross-party support responding to the PwC and Tax Practitioners Board issue demonstrates the lack of seriousness from the Government towards this legislation; and* >> >> *(b) calls on the Government to support the Opposition's proposals to acknowledge its own Future Gas Strategy and support the future of the gas industry\".*","result":"negative","slug":"division-federal-senate-8925","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2024-05-16/32"}
